---
id: org.dxos.plugin.github.sync
name: GitHub polling sync
version: 0.1.0
---

Efficient polling sync of GitHub repositories and pull requests into ECHO, over one object model.

This is part 1 of a three-part design; each part ships on its own:

| Part | Spec                                              | Needs                          |
|------|---------------------------------------------------|--------------------------------|
| 1    | This document                                     | Nothing                        |
| 2    | [Two-way file sync](FILE-SYNC.mdl)                | Part 1's binding on `Repo`     |
| 3    | [Event dispatch](../../plugin-connector/spec/EVENTS.mdl) | Part 1's sync operation |

A bound repository is polled every few minutes. A poll that finds nothing costs one conditional
request, which GitHub answers `304 Not Modified` without charging the rate limit; a poll that finds
changes costs two in the common case (one page of changes, at most 100 pull requests). Once implemented, this document replaces F-4 and F-5 of [PLUGIN.mdl](../PLUGIN.mdl).

## Extensions

The following extension dialects are used in this document.
Each extension is defined in the Appendix or resolved via its URI.

| Term        | URI                            |
|-------------|--------------------------------|
| `type`      | `org.dxos.mdl.type@1.0`        |
| `service`   | `org.dxos.mdl.service@1.0`     |
